## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical design of multilingual, budget-aware Azure AI pipelines with safety and observability in a real-world support scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Multilingual real-time translation
- PII redaction and data safety guardrails
- Tenant-specific policy via Key Vault classifications
- Token budget gating and fallback UX
- Grounding on a versioned KB with Cognitive Search
- Drift detection and retraining via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: redaction + budget gate
function prepareQuery(input, tenantId) {
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const translated = translate(redacted, 'en');
  const budget = getTenantBudget(tenantId);
  if (wouldExceedBudget(budget, estimatedTokens(translated))) {
    return { fallback: true, type: 'diagnostic' };
  }
  return { query: translated, tenantId };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test translation accuracy and redaction quality at scale?
- What metrics and dashboards would you expose in Azure Monitor for drift and budget violations?

## Why This Is Asked

This tests design for guardrails, data isolation, and cost controls in Azure OpenAI deployments, a common advanced requirement for regulated customers.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic safety policy engine
- Prompt redaction and blocking
- API Management routing
- Grounding with versioned KB (Blob + Cognitive Search)
- Per-tenant isolation (Cosmos DB) and quotas
- Telemetry and auditing (Data Lake)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal policy eval
function evaluatePrompt(prompt, policies) {
  for (const p of policies) {
    if (p.types?.some(t => prompt.includes(t))) {
      return {blocked: true, reason: p.reason}
    }
  }
  // simple redact example
  const redacted = prompt.replace(/SSN-\d{4}/g, '[REDACTED_SSN]')
  return {blocked: false, redacted}
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement per-tenant billing and quotas at API level?
- How would you test guardrails under burst traffic?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a practical, beginner-friendly multi-tenant flow with prompt catalog versioning, failover, and privacy controls in Azure OpenAI.

## Key Concepts

- API Management routing with tenant context
- Versioned prompt catalog stored in Azure Blob
- Per-tenant quotas and graceful fallback
- PII redaction via Text Analytics before OpenAI calls
- Regional OpenAI endpoints and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
async function routeRequest(tenantId, payload) {
  const tmpl = await blob.get(`prompts/${tenantId}/v1.json`);
  const redacted = pii.redact(payload.prompt, payload.user);
  const finalPrompt = `${tmpl.promptPrefix}\n${redacted}`;
  return openai.chat(finalPrompt);
}
```

